<p>I believe I have to echo the point made here. I don't really see the Foundation as being a negligent entity especially when it comes to containment of a SCP. I don't really buy the angle that it would be to insignificant for them to care about. As for the the money angle, I really don't understand where that was going. All that being said, without making wholesale changes, which I wouldn't expect you to do of course, I doubt minor tweaks will be enough for me to change my vote on the article. However, I would recommend changing the water temperature to -1.8°C. That is the coldest the water ever gets in the Arctic Ocean. Any colder would just freeze the water, circulation or not.</p>

