<p>This is one of the most incompetent portrayals of the Foundation I've ever seen. Receiving a series of direct emails about a Keter class anomaly that's kicking everyone's ass for months and months, and they can't even manage to acknowledge or send one reply; let alone think to resolve the issue. And it's explained away, not by depicting a small-scale Foundation without the available resources themselves; but by a Foundation apparently just too big and self-important to care.</p>
<p>The fines thing confuses me too. Is this something the Foundation has typically done before? How do they enforce payment of fines; do they have an appeals court for disputed infractions; is there any neutral arbitration? Or is this extortion bit meant to make the Foundation come off as cruel villains in this piece? Because if you're saying that the Foundation were deliberately ignoring the situation as it played out, then this potentially reads to me like some kind of convoluted caroonish scheme to get rid of Wilson's by driving them to bankruptcy. But I'm doubtful that was the intent.</p>
<p>(P.S.: -5° C is below freezing, even for salt water.)</p>

