														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840937">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A hospital, in a relatively populated area. Anyone who is sick, or injured, that walks in, will start to recover or heal, across the course of a few days to a few months, depending. Non-human life mutates, as if it's trying to become human, and ends up dead. Broken or damaged artificial objects 'heal' over with human biological components. 'Nurse' entities appear as body disposal, and to move immobile 'patients' to a bed. Where they come from is unknown, but they don't heal, they just don't die.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> On the worldbuilding side, this'll be in a relatively populated area, and may require not only fancy containment procedures, due to the hospital keeping itself looking in working order, and sending out &quot;appointment&quot; letters to the local area, somehow aware of illness or injury within a certain radius of it. Given its location, it may also require cooperation with a GoI, or local authorities, or some sort of group outside of the foundation. Perhaps it got discovered by two at a roughly similar time, or otherwise the foundation had it first, but then some other group (likely the GOC given they are, to my knowledge, the most able to show their faces in public, or the UIU if I put this in the states) turns up.</p>
<p>Experiment wise, it'll probably be a case of them trying to see how far it'll go, finding it can cure anomalous diseases (if the patient is still alive and human), and injuries, as well as things not thought fixable by modern medicine. Perhaps implication of some researcher using it for personal use, and getting into a lot of trouble for it, along with the expected D-Class abuse to see just what this thing can heal. Some stuff as well with the nurses, finding they're non-hostile, but trying to figure out where they come from, only to discover they're the patients that don't make it, put together into the nurses, and animated by unknown means.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I'd like to think the hospital itself is pretty unique, but I'd also use this as a sort of way of tying a few other SCPs together, those that are disease based, or cause funky injuries, and how the hospital tries to &quot;fix&quot; them. The slower time scale means that whilst telling why things are healing is impossible, observing what specifically is happening isn't. The nurses being non-hostile and non-belligerent also aids to this, since they can just put researchers in there with the D-Class to see what happens day by day.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This is the first SCP I'll have ever tried to write. I've been reading for a good while, but my knowledge isn't encyclopaedic. Any ideas off of the vaguer points here would be greatly appreciated, and again I'm very sorry if this is too close to something that already exists.</p>

