<p>Goo Goo Gaa Gaa, Baby Crit Here</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hold&nbsp;all&nbsp;my&nbsp;baby&nbsp;calls&nbsp;baby&nbsp;Helen</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Ahem</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Maybe even some mentions of SCPs that were exterminated using this SCP. Potential for cross-links.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I recoiled when I saw this. Oh boy is that a bad idea. Neutralized SCPs already have reasons give, so this is an idea that won't work, so I suggest scraping that part.</p>
<p>About the doors and the cube, can they be broken or are they indestructible? Is it possible to hold the door open? What happens if you put an inanimate object in there? Ask yourself similar questions and put them in, it will help flesh out your concept.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I think it would be cool having some more non-euclidian geometry on the site, plus some actively hostile non-euclidian structures.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, this wouldn't qualify an a hostile structure, for 1. That would entail it actively trying to kill them the entire time. Also, non-euclidian geometry is not that rare. Several other anomalous buildings and others have non-eucldian geometry.</p>
<p>Overall, the concept seems a tad boring. Nothing really pops out at me. I suggest adding some kind of twist with where the vanished people go.</p>
<p>I don't do recrits, so don't PM me, thanks.</p>
</div>
